# Code owners
#
# The integration plan's execution-risk table names "ownership without
# authority" as a live risk, with the mitigation "add each owner to
# CODEOWNERS". That mitigation had never been carried out: the ten domain
# owners (D-1 .. D-10) were used throughout the standards, the toleration
# ledger and the plan, and nothing connected them to a required review.
#
# THE OWNER HANDLES BELOW ARE PLACEHOLDERS. A placeholder like
# @econojin/platform-team is worse than having no CODEOWNERS at all: GitHub
# resolves an unknown owner to nobody and requires no review, while the file
# still looks configured. Replace every handle with a real team or account
# before relying on this. tests/contract/test_codeowners.py refuses obvious
# placeholder spellings but cannot tell whether a handle resolves.
#
# The D-ids match the source-of-truth table in
# docs/INTEGRATION_STANDARDIZATION_PLAN_FA_2026-09-28.md and the owner field in
# docs/standards/tolerated-degradations.yaml. tests/contract/test_codeowners.py
# checks the three stay in step.

